# Page 3 analytics
story += [P('2. Analytics and user workflows','H1X'), P('The standard workflow is: load data, check the detected source and readiness, run the analysis from its page, then review results and run history. Batch runs are asynchronous and persisted in PostgreSQL.','BodyX'), P('Dashboard','H2X'), P('Shows overall sales, order and customer metrics, average order value, repeat purchase rate and cancellation measures, plus time trends, top products, and geographic breakdowns. Amount formatting follows the selected source currency (BRL for Olist, GBP for UCI).','BodyX'), P('Customers and RFM','H2X'), P('RFM measures Recency (days since last purchase), Frequency (distinct orders), and Monetary (spend). Scores are assigned by quintiles; recency scoring is reversed so recent customers receive higher scores. Rule-based segments include Champions, Loyal Customers, Potential Loyalists, New Customers, Need Attention, About to Sleep, At Risk, Can\'t Lose Them, and Hibernating.','BodyX'), P('Customer segmentation','H2X'), P('K-Means clusters customers using recency, frequency, and monetary values. The implementation log-transforms skewed values, standardizes features, evaluates candidate cluster counts using silhouette score, and saves cluster profiles and a PCA projection for visualization. The candidate range is k=2 through k=8, bounded by the number of customers.','BodyX'), P('Products and baskets','H2X'), P('Apriori mines products that occur together in an order and produces association rules. Support is the share of baskets containing an itemset; confidence estimates P(B given A); lift compares that confidence with the baseline frequency of B. For bounded memory use, the analysis limits input to up to 150 frequent products and itemsets of length at most 3.','BodyX'), P('Forecasting','H2X'), P('Forecasting aggregates revenue by day and compares a Gradient Boosting model with a seasonal-naive baseline. It holds out the final 28 days for evaluation, uses revenue lags (28, 35, and 42 days) plus shifted rolling/calendar features, reports MAE and RMSE, then refits on available history for a forecast horizon up to 28 days. These are historical-data forecasts, not guarantees.','BodyX'), P('Run history','H2X'), P('Analytics runs have a type and status (pending, running, completed, or failed), parameters, timestamps, duration, and saved results. The Run History page makes previous work and failures inspectable.','BodyX'), PageBreak()]
